{"id": "EUVD-2026-91136", "enisaUuid": "f6356ed0-0dfd-3adf-9901-0d552a0385ed", "description": "Mooncake transfer engine before 0.3.13 contains an untrusted pointer dereference in ServerSession::readHeader that allows unauthenticated attackers to read and write arbitrary process memory via the TCP transport data port. Attackers can send a crafted SessionHeader with arbitrary addr and size values using READ or WRITE opcodes to disclose KV cache contents, prompts and secrets or corrupt memory toward code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T23:19:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T18:22:06", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake/issues/4441", "https://github.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake/commit/a2933849417259e562fc9cbad63c618d464dfb2d", "https://github.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake/releases/tag/v0.3.13", "https://github.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake/blob/6041a609a8c3af35e778f70db344f145c2914980/mooncake-transfer-engine/src/transport/tcp_transport/tcp_transport.cpp#L209", "https://github.com/kvcache-ai/Mooncake", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mooncake-transfer-engine-before-0.3.13-unauthenticated-arbitrary-memory-read-write-via-tcp-transport"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103764", "GHSA-mp8g-r7h2-5x36"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4736cfc1-474b-3de4-bcba-ff601277a7d2", "product": {"name": "mooncake", "vendor": {"name": "kvcache-ai"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.3.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "12efdfda-8e1e-374c-9c7d-cc1b88fa2f7c", "vendor": {"name": "kvcache-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}